  user_input {
    user_response: "Create a complete, polished HTML5 Canvas puzzle game called **NEON BLOCK**.\n\nThe game should be an original combination of a tile-merging puzzle and a block-placement puzzle.\n\n**Core requirements:**\n- Single-player offline gameplay.\n- Responsive landscape-first design for Android tablets.\n- Dark background with premium neon graphics.\n- Smooth animations and satisfying visual effects.\n- Touchscreen support.\n- Keyboard arrow keys, Enter and Space support.\n- Prepare controls for future Amazon Fire TV D-pad compatibility.\n- Score, best score and game-over screen.\n- Save high scores locally.\n- Pause, restart and sound toggle.\n- Generate sound effects using Web Audio API.\n- No external APIs, external CDNs, login or online dependencies.\n- No Google Play Services.\n\n**Design:**\nCreate a premium arcade interface with glowing blue, purple and cyan tiles, clean typography, subtle gradients and polished transitions.\n\n**Technical requirements:**\n- Use HTML5 Canvas and JavaScript.\n- Keep the game self-contained.\n- Do not use copyrighted game assets.\n- Handle different screen sizes without clipping.\n- Include clear instructions for players.\n- Make all buttons functional.\n- Avoid placeholder functionality.\n\nBuild the complete playable game, not just a prototype or visual mockup.\n\nBefore finishing, test the game logic, tile movement, scoring, collision detection, game-over conditions and restart functionality."
    items {
      item {
        text_block {
          content: "---\ntype: \"feature\"\ntitle: \"Create a game\"\nicon: \"sports_esports\"\n---\n\nI want to build an interactive game in this app. If the game is 3D (or a spatial/depth-heavy genre where 3D fits best), you **MUST** use the `threejs` skill (`/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md`). Otherwise, if the game is 2D, board, card, puzzle, or casual (or an unspecified game where 2D fits naturally), you **MUST** use the `frontend-design` skill (`/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`) and you **MUST** read its 2D games reference (`/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/4_games_2d_casual.md`).\n\nFollow these core game craft guidelines:\n- **Game Shell & Title Screen**: Use a full-viewport Game Shell (`Title Screen` -> `Playing` -> `Pause / Victory / Game Over` modal) \342\200\224 never render website navbars or footers. Stage an atmospheric live-world camera pan, interactive hero centerpiece, live board/table, or illustrated key-art backdrop (`generate_image`) on the Title Screen with a bespoke inline `<svg>` title lockup over 30\342\200\22340% calm negative space (or in a dedicated side panel beside a live board), a primary Start CTA (`Enter`/`Space` or click to start), and a single flat control-hint line matched to the genre (e.g., `WASD Move \302\267 Space Action \302\267 Esc Pause` for real-time/arcade games, or click/drag/keyboard shortcuts for turn-based, board, card, and puzzle games).\n- **World-Matched, Low-Occlusion UI**: Keep at least 85% of the playfield or game board unobstructed (`pointer-events: none` on HUD overlay wrappers; never use `backdrop-filter` over an active WebGL/Canvas viewport). Style perimeter status clusters and custom `<svg>` icons in the game world\'s own palette with `tabular-nums` integer readouts.\n- **60fps Simulation & Responsive Input (or DOM/CSS Board & Grid Layouts)**: For 3D, real-time, or arcade games, mount the `<canvas>` in an isolated container so React state updates never re-render the game loop, clamp frame delta time (`Math.min(rawDt, 0.05)`), separate continuous `held` inputs from edge-triggered `justPressed` actions (with input buffering and coyote time where applicable), and clear held keys on window blur. For 2D turn-based, board, card, word, and puzzle games, use responsive DOM/CSS/SVG board, card-table, or `>= 44px` interactive grid layouts with clear valid-move highlights and `<= 200ms` compositor-only transitions (`transform`, `opacity`).\n- **Game Feel & Encounter/Progression Design**: Trigger weight-scaled visual and procedural Web Audio synth feedback on core actions with a mute toggle. For real-time or arcade games, include hit flashes, brief 30\342\200\22380ms simulation hitstop on heavy impacts, decaying camera shake, pooled particle bursts, squash-and-stretch, and distinct enemy/hazard behaviors with visible windup telegraphs and a smooth difficulty ramp. For turn-based, card, board, and puzzle games, pair crisp move/capture/flip animations with clear turn, rule, or multi-tier hint states and round progression."
        }
      }
    }
    items {
      text: "Create a complete, polished HTML5 Canvas puzzle game called **NEON BLOCK**.\n\nThe game should be an original combination of a tile-merging puzzle and a block-placement puzzle.\n\n**Core requirements:**\n- Single-player offline gameplay.\n- Responsive landscape-first design for Android tablets.\n- Dark background with premium neon graphics.\n- Smooth animations and satisfying visual effects.\n- Touchscreen support.\n- Keyboard arrow keys, Enter and Space support.\n- Prepare controls for future Amazon Fire TV D-pad compatibility.\n- Score, best score and game-over screen.\n- Save high scores locally.\n- Pause, restart and sound toggle.\n- Generate sound effects using Web Audio API.\n- No external APIs, external CDNs, login or online dependencies.\n- No Google Play Services.\n\n**Design:**\nCreate a premium arcade interface with glowing blue, purple and cyan tiles, clean typography, subtle gradients and polished transitions.\n\n**Technical requirements:**\n- Use HTML5 Canvas and JavaScript.\n- Keep the game self-contained.\n- Do not use copyrighted game assets.\n- Handle different screen sizes without clipping.\n- Include clear instructions for players.\n- Make all buttons functional.\n- Avoid placeholder functionality.\n\nBuild the complete playable game, not just a prototype or visual mockup.\n\nBefore finishing, test the game logic, tile movement, scoring, collision detection, game-over conditions and restart functionality."
    }
  }
}
