    thinking: "**Developing Test Suite**\n\nI\'m currently focused on constructing a comprehensive automated test script. The goal is to rigorously test collision detection, bounds checking, tile placement, and scoring accuracy. I\'m prioritizing edge cases, such as out-of-bounds anchor points and overlapping placements, to ensure robust functionality. I plan to use `npx tsx` and `run_command` to efficiently execute the test suite.\n\n\n**Refining Gameplay Logic**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the core gameplay mechanics, specifically how points are calculated for piece placement. I\'m focusing on the 3+ tile merging system, including cascading chain merges that double the value of upgraded tiles. Row and column clearing mechanics are being integrated, along with tray refill and guaranteed playable fallback logic. I\'ve also focused on game-over detection and am currently verifying game state with `npx tsx -e`. I\'m now testing layout responsiveness on various screen sizes.\n\n\n"
