  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Skill Relevancy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the relevancy of `frontend-design`. I\'ve already processed `SKILL.md` and `references/4_games_2d_casual.md`, and now I\'m connecting the dots to see exactly how this skill set factors into the current request. Specifically, I\'m evaluating the fit between the design implications of this request, and this skill.\n\n\n**Evaluating Design Priorities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific design requirements. I\'m prioritizing zero-pill discipline, smooth transitions, and clean typography as core elements. I\'m also examining the need for `44px+` touch targets and tabular numbers. These details are paramount to maintaining the clean aesthetic and usability of **NEON BLOCK**. I\'ve determined that no other skills are directly relevant, considering offline and local storage constraints. I\'m proceeding to carefully review the upgrade request to ensure the Daily Challenge System integrates seamlessly.\n\n\n**Defining Challenge Tiers**\n\nI\'m now establishing the core difficulty levels for the Daily Challenge system: Standard, Hard, and Expert. Each tier will feature distinct objectives. I\'m focusing on defining the objectives, rewards, and the optional pre-seeded board layouts. The goal is to make each daily challenge feel like a unique and engaging experience. I\'m also considering seeded RNG for each challenge.\n\n\n**Refining Reward System**\n\nI\'m now implementing the daily streak and rewards system. I\'m focusing on ensuring victory conditions trigger immediately and that rewards are granted flawlessly. To prevent reward duplication, I\'m integrating checks for completed dates and reward claims. I\'m also planning to implement a celebratory banner for daily challenge completion.\n\n\n**Implementing Local Storage**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating local storage for the daily challenge system. I\'m storing `streak`, `lastCompletedDate`, `totalShards`, and `completedDates` within `neon_block_daily_v1`. I\'ve implemented the streak logic, ensuring it correctly handles consecutive days, missed days, and first-time completions. I\'m also ensuring best score, progress, completion status, reward claimed status, and attempts are all saved locally. I\'m proceeding to create a dedicated screen for these challenges.\n\n\n**Designing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing specific UI elements for the Daily Challenge screen, sidebar, and pause/game over views. I will display today\'s date, the challenge title, and difficulty. Also, the objective and progress bar, reward information, and streak stats, as well as a 7-day calendar strip and key buttons are under consideration. During gameplay, a compact tracker in the sidebar will show objective progress. Next, I\'ll be implementing advanced particle visual effects with a pooled particle engine optimized for mobile and tablets and a hard particle budget.\n\n\n**Optimizing Particle Effects**\n\nI\'m now determining ideal particle effect configurations. I\'m focusing on responsiveness based on device and user preference for reduced motion. I\'m prioritizing visually distinct and rich particle shapes and behaviors. Specifically, I\'m designing particle effects that correspond with actions like merging tiles, combos, clearing lines, and high-score celebrations. These should be visually engaging without being distracting. I\'m aiming for optimized mobile performance with hard particle budgets. I\'ll need to define different visual behaviors to match different events.\n\n\n**Enhancing Visual Feedback**\n\nI\'m now integrating enhanced visual feedback. I\'m focusing on \"Neon Fireworks\" effects during high-score celebrations and game-over events, ensuring they\'re multi-stage and visually dynamic. I\'m also implementing smooth transitions with CSS compositor and subtle screen shake for combos and line clears, always respecting the user\'s \"prefers-reduced-motion\" setting. I\'m adding particle intensity settings, allowing users to tune the visual density through an interactive toggle, persisted locally.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Effects**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific sound and visual events. I\'m synchronizing \"Daily Challenge Complete\" fanfare, and \"Combo chord swells\" with merge ghost landing and shockwave expansion. I\'m also ensuring full respect for reduced motion preferences, disabling effects, and ensuring minimal transitions for a clean experience when this setting is active. I\'m proceeding to inspect the existing files to be updated and new ones to be created, and adding the sound effects.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_3779437209834362619"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export const GRID_SIZE = 6;\\nexport const TRAY_SIZE = 3;\\n\\nexport type GameMode = \'CLASSIC\' | \'DAILY\';\\n\\nexport type GameStatus =\\n  | \'TITLE_MENU\'\\n  | \'DAILY_SCREEN\'\\n  | \'PLAYING\'\\n  | \'PAUSED\'\\n  | \'GAME_OVER\';\\n\\nexport type FocusZone = \'GRID\' | \'TRAY\';\\n\\nexport type ParticleIntensity = \'LOW\' | \'MEDIUM\' | \'HIGH\';\\n\\nexport type DailyDifficulty = \'STANDARD\' | \'HARD\' | \'EXPERT\';\\n\\nexport type DailyObjectiveType = \'SCORE\' | \'MAX_TILE\' | \'LINES\' | \'MERGES\';\\n\\nexport interface DailyChallengeConfig {\\n  dateKey: string; // Local YYYY-MM-DD\\n  seed: number;\\n  title: string;\\n  difficulty: DailyDifficulty;\\n  objectiveType: DailyObjectiveType;\\n  targetValue: number;\\n  description: string;\\n  rewardShards: number;\\n  starterCells: { r: number; c: number; value: number }[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface DailyDayRecord {\\n  dateKey: string;\\n  completed: boolean;\\n  rewardClaimed: boolean;\\n  bestProgress: number;\\n  bestScore: number;\\n  attempts: number;\\n  completedAt?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface DailySaveState {\\n  currentStreak: number;\\n  longestStreak: number;\\n  lastCompletedDate: string | null;\\n  totalShards: number;\\n  records: Record<string, DailyDayRecord>;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface GridCoord {\\n  r: number;\\n  c: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CellOffset {\\n  dr: number;\\n  dc: number;\\n  value: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface BlockPiece {\\n  id: string;\\n  shapeName: string;\\n  cells: CellOffset[];\\n  width: number;\\n  height: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface BoardTile {\\n  id: number;\\n  value: number;\\n  scale: number;\\n  targetScale: number;\\n  offsetX: number;\\n  offsetY: number;\\n  flash: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport type GridMatrix = (BoardTile | null)[][];\\n\\nexport interface MergeStep {\\n  fromCells: GridCoord[];\\n  targetCell: GridCoord;\\n  oldValue: number;\\n  newValue: number;\\n  comboDepth: number;\\n  points: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LineClearStep {\\n  rows: number[];\\n  cols: number[];\\n  clearedCells: { r: number; c: number; value: number }[];\\n  points: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface PlacementPreview {\\n  valid: boolean;\\n  anchorRow: number;\\n  anchorCol: number;\\n  targetCells: GridCoord[];\\n  willMergeCells: GridCoord[];\\n  willClearRows: number[];\\n  willClearCols: number[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface TurnResolution {\\n  placedCells: GridCoord[];\\n  placementPoints: number;\\n  mergeSteps: MergeStep[];\\n  lineClearStep: LineClearStep | null;\\n  totalPointsGained: number;\\n  maxComboDepth: number;\\n  newMaxTile: number;\\n  refilledTray: boolean;\\n  isGameOver: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface GameStats {\\n  score: number;\\n  bestScore: number;\\n  maxTile: number;\\n  mergesCount: number;\\n  linesCleared: number;\\n  bestCombo: number;\\n  turnsPlayed: number;\\n  isNewBest: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport type ParticleShape = \'circle\' | \'spark\' | \'diamond\';\\n\\nexport interface Particle {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  size: number;\\n  color: string;\\n  alpha: number;\\n  life: number;\\n  maxLife: number;\\n  shape: ParticleShape;\\n  gravity: number;\\n  drag: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface FireworkRocket {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  vx: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  targetY: number;\\n  color: string;\\n  trailTimer: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ShockwaveRing {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  radius: number;\\n  maxRadius: number;\\n  color: string;\\n  alpha: number;\\n  life: number;\\n  maxLife: number;\\n  lineWidth: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LineBeam {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  w: number;\\n  h: number;\\n  color: string;\\n  life: number;\\n  maxLife: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface FloatingText {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  vy: number;\\n  text: string;\\n  subtext?: string;\\n  color: string;\\n  life: number;\\n  maxLife: n