  planner_response {
    response: "**NEON BLOCK** has been upgraded with the Daily Challenge system, advanced particle visual effects, and responsive polish while keeping all existing Classic gameplay, scoring, controls, and saved high scores intact and 100% offline.\n\n### Summary of Upgrades\n\n1. **Daily Challenge System**\n   - **Local Calendar Seeding**: Generates a deterministic daily puzzle (`YYYY-MM-DD` local time) with a unique starter grid, piece deal sequence, title, difficulty tier (`Standard`, `Hard`, `Expert`), objective (`Score`, `Max Tile`, `Lines`, or `Merges`), and Neon Shard reward.\n   - **Dedicated Daily Challenge Screen**: Accessible from the Title Screen, sidebar/header, and Game Over modal, displaying today\'s objective progress bar, difficulty, reward status, active/best streak counters, total Neon Shards, and a 7-day completion strip.\n   - **Streaks & Duplicate-Reward Prevention**: Tracks consecutive daily completions and saves progress locally in `localStorage`; replaying an already-completed day lets you improve your score without awarding duplicate shards or double-counting your streak.\n\n2. **Advanced Particle Visual Effects**\n   - **Multi-Shape Pooled Particle Engine**: Uses directional `spark` streaks, `diamond` shards, and glowing `circle` particles with additive blending and smooth quadratic fade-out, capped by a mobile-friendly particle budget (`Low`: 90, `Medium`: 185, `High`: 360).\n   - **Merges, Combos & Line Shockwaves**: Merging tiles emit palette-matched neon bursts; multi-step chain combos (`\303\2272+`) trigger colorful multi-hue explosions and double shockwaves; clearing full rows or columns fires plasma beams with expanding shockwave rings.\n   - **Ambient Motes & High-Score Fireworks**: Twinkling background particles drift behind the board, and breaking your Best Score or completing a Daily Challenge launches rising firework rockets that burst into cascading sparkler blooms.\n\n3. **Polish & Accessibility**\n   - **Particle Intensity Settings**: Adjustable `Low` / `Med` / `High` segmented control in both the landscape sidebar and the Pause modal (persisted locally).\n   - **Synchronized Audio & Screen Shake**: Web Audio API firework bursts and Daily Challenge completion fanfares synchronize with visual detonations, paired with decaying micro screen shake on major combos and line clears.\n   - **Reduced Motion & Smooth Transitions**: Smooth `160ms` modal/screen transitions and full `prefers-reduced-motion` support (disables screen shake, fireworks, and excess particle storms when enabled).\n\n### Verification\n- `compile_applet` (`vite build`) succeeded.\n- `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- Automated `tsx` verification tests passed for deterministic daily generation, daily starter playability, streak increments/resets, duplicate-reward prevention, cascading merges, line clears, collision checks, and responsive landscape/portrait Canvas layouts."
    modified_response: "**NEON BLOCK** has been upgraded with the Daily Challenge system, advanced particle visual effects, and responsive polish while keeping all existing Classic gameplay, scoring, controls, and saved high scores intact and 100% offline.\n\n### Summary of Upgrades\n\n1. **Daily Challenge System**\n   - **Local Calendar Seeding**: Generates a deterministic daily puzzle (`YYYY-MM-DD` local time) with a unique starter grid, piece deal sequence, title, difficulty tier (`Standard`, `Hard`, `Expert`), objective (`Score`, `Max Tile`, `Lines`, or `Merges`), and Neon Shard reward.\n   - **Dedicated Daily Challenge Screen**: Accessible from the Title Screen, sidebar/header, and Game Over modal, displaying today\'s objective progress bar, difficulty, reward status, active/best streak counters, total Neon Shards, and a 7-day completion strip.\n   - **Streaks & Duplicate-Reward Prevention**: Tracks consecutive daily completions and saves progress locally in `localStorage`; replaying an already-completed day lets you improve your score without awarding duplicate shards or double-counting your streak.\n\n2. **Advanced Particle Visual Effects**\n   - **Multi-Shape Pooled Particle Engine**: Uses directional `spark` streaks, `diamond` shards, and glowing `circle` particles with additive blending and smooth quadratic fade-out, capped by a mobile-friendly particle budget (`Low`: 90, `Medium`: 185, `High`: 360).\n   - **Merges, Combos & Line Shockwaves**: Merging tiles emit palette-matched neon bursts; multi-step chain combos (`\303\2272+`) trigger colorful multi-hue explosions and double shockwaves; clearing full rows or columns fires plasma beams with expanding shockwave rings.\n   - **Ambient Motes & High-Score Fireworks**: Twinkling background particles drift behind the board, and breaking your Best Score or completing a Daily Challenge launches rising firework rockets that burst into cascading sparkler blooms.\n\n3. **Polish & Accessibility**\n   - **Particle Intensity Settings**: Adjustable `Low` / `Med` / `High` segmented control in both the landscape sidebar and the Pause modal (persisted locally).\n   - **Synchronized Audio & Screen Shake**: Web Audio API firework bursts and Daily Challenge completion fanfares synchronize with visual detonations, paired with decaying micro screen shake on major combos and line clears.\n   - **Reduced Motion & Smooth Transitions**: Smooth `160ms` modal/screen transitions and full `prefers-reduced-motion` support (disables screen shake, fireworks, and excess particle storms when enabled).\n\n### Verification\n- `compile_applet` (`vite build`) succeeded.\n- `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- Automated `tsx` verification tests passed for deterministic daily generation, daily starter playability, streak increments/resets, duplicate-reward prevention, cascading merges, line clears, collision checks, and responsive landscape/portrait Canvas layouts."
