  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Edge Cases Clearly**\n\nI\'ve got a grasp of the discovered edge cases. Focusing on the `\'H\'` key, it currently activates the \"How to Play\" modal *only* when the game status is `\'TITLE_MENU\'`. The implications of this are now fully apparent, and I\'m analyzing each one carefully.\n\n\n**Clarifying Interaction Details**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the specifics of the \'H\' key interaction. It\'s now apparent that the \"How to Play\" modal *only* opens from the `\'TITLE_MENU\'`. Critically, it *doesn\'t* open from `\'PLAYING\'`, `\'PAUSED\'`, `\'GAME_OVER\'`, `\'DAILY_SCREEN\'`, or `\'DASHBOARD\'`. I\'m also ensuring that pressing \'H\' when the modal is open, or pressing Escape, cleanly closes it and returns the user to the previous view. I\'m taking a close look at how `NeonCanvas` responds, and how to prevent keydown event bubbling during the display of `showHelp`. I\'m going to determine whether to simply ignore keyboard events or specifically disable `Escape` and `H` when `showHelp` is active.\n\n\n**Refining Focus Behavior**\n\nI\'m now refining the focus and closure behavior of the \'How to Play\' modal. Closing the modal using \'Escape\', \'H\', or the close button returns focus to the canvas when in the \'PLAYING\' state, or back to the menu. I\'m also ensuring that the backdrop click will also close the modal. \'H\' now ignores modifier keys and text input to prevent conflicts. Lastly, I\'m considering the potential interaction with the `DashboardScreen`, especially when other sub-modals are present.\n\n\n"
