  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Current State**\n\nI\'ve noticed how cleanly the `NeonCanvas` component handles disabling user input when the game isn\'t running. Specifically, it uses a `statusRef` to check and prevent both pointer drag/tap interactions and canvas keyboard input when the game `status` is not `\'PLAYING\'`. This streamlined approach provides an intuitive user experience.\n\n\n**Analyzing Input Protection**\n\nI\'ve realized that the `NeonCanvas` component effectively protects the board during the \"How to Play\" modal. Passing a conditional `status` to `<NeonCanvas />` allows the overlay to gracefully pause interaction, dim the board, and perfectly restore the game state upon dismissal. Removing duplicate key handlers in `NeonCanvas` further eliminates potential bugs and streamlines key handling.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Escape Handling**\n\nI\'m solidifying the `Escape` key handling within `DashboardScreen` when the `claimCelebration` modal is active. To ensure the modal closes before navigating the menu, a capture-phase `keydown` listener is added only when `claimCelebration` is showing. A check for `isHelpOpen` prevents conflicts. If `claimCelebration` is showing, I want the event to be consumed by the capture phase, preventing unintended menu navigation.\n\n\n**Tracing Modal Interactions**\n\nNow, I\'m tracing the interactions between the `claimCelebration` modal and other elements. I\'ve mapped out scenarios involving the `Escape` key, including cases with the \"How to Play\" modal. Pressing `Escape` while `claimCelebration` is open now correctly closes the modal, preventing unintended navigation, and returns to the previous menu state! I\'ve also noted that `confirmClear`\'s behavior within the Combo History tab with Escape could be investigated for interactions.\n\n\n**Defining Navigation States**\n\nI\'m now defining the structure of `/src/game/navigation.ts`, starting with a clear `NavigationState` interface: `{ status: GameStatus; history: GameStatus[] }`. The initial state will be `TITLE_MENU` with an empty history. I\'m focusing on crafting pure transition functions, such as `navigateToView`, and verifying every view transition with thorough unit tests. I\'m specifically aiming to make sure the Escape key navigates correctly across all views.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation History**\n\nI\'m now refining the history management for game navigation, especially when transitioning mid-game to screens like the dashboard or daily screen. Pressing `Escape` in these cases will return safely. I\'m carefully managing the history stack to accurately represent navigation flow. Restarting a game from a paused or game over state ensures clean navigation. The initial state is the root `TITLE_MENU` with an empty history. I\'m focusing on ensuring restarting keeps originating menus at the top of history.\n\n\n**Implementing Navigation Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the state transition logic within `/src/game/navigation.ts`. I\'m handling game over and pausing. I\'m taking care of managing the history when the game ends, as well as preserving a safe root to return to, by stripping \'PLAYING\' states.\n\n\n**Defining Back Behavior**\n\nI\'m now defining the behavior for `GoBack`/`Backspace` interactions across different menus and screens. The logic handles navigating from various states, including `\'TITLE_MENU\'`, `\'PLAYING\'`, `\'PAUSED\'`, `\'DAILY_SCREEN\'`, `\'DASHBOARD\'`, and `\'GAME_OVER\'`. I\'m using `state.history` to manage navigation. When at the title menu or in active gameplay, there is no change. Otherwise, it pops from history. If history is empty, I ensure a safe return to a known state such as the title or playing.\n\nI\'m now tracing every scenario!\n\n\n**Tracing Navigation Flow**\n\nI\'m now tracing the precise navigation flow. Specifically, I am focusing on detailed scenarios with the help overlay to ensure the board state is restored, regardless of where I was. I\'m making sure that pressing Escape or the help key now opens and closes the overlay correctly, and always returns me to a sane state. For example, I\'m ensuring pressing `Escape` in a `PLAYING` state while `Help` is open returns to `PLAYING`.\n\n\n**Verifying Navigation Transitions**\n\nNow, I\'m verifying the navigation transitions with thorough scenarios to confirm the expected behavior. I\'ve focused on various game states and key presses. I\'ve confirmed that the Escape key correctly navigates back from states such as game over, dashboard, daily screen, and paused game, always returning to the correct previous state. I\'m testing navigation between classic game and daily game, after the daily game has ended. I\'m also ensuring pressing Escape on dashboard during a paused state returns to the game.\n\n\n**Confirming Edge Case Logic**\n\nI\'m now confirming the logic is fully robust across all views and interactions. Keyboard focus restoration is confirmed, including focus management from help overlay. I\'m also addressing how the \"How to Play\" overlay presents, by ensuring all underlying views remain mounted. The focus on robust handling across all cases continues!\n\n\n**Enhancing User Experience**\n\nI\'m now integrating a backdrop click-to-close handler and setting `aria-modal=\"true\"` to ensure the \"How to Play\" overlay maintains state, and smooth transitions when toggling. I\'m adding clear keyboard shortcuts (H/Esc) within the modal, and updating the keyboard controls. I\'m also including `H Help \302\267 Esc Back` hints on the Title Screen and Sidebar.\n\n\n"
