  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Seamless Integration**\n\nI\'m now meticulously planning the integration of both requested features into the existing NEON BLOCK architecture. The goal is a perfect fit: complete preservation of current gameplay, data, and features, meeting all requirements, and passing every regression test.\n\n\n**Refining Streak Implementation**\n\nI\'m deep in the specifics of the streak logic. I\'ve designed a dedicated module (`src/game/streaks.ts`) to handle persistence and date management. I\'m focusing on the qualification rules: streaks increment only upon Daily Challenge completion or Daily Reward Milestone. I\'m building a robust system to avoid multiple increments per day, using a deduplicated and sorted list of completed dates.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Data Integrity**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data persistence. I\'ve decided on a dedicated versioned key, `neon_block_streak_v1`, for storing streak data. This approach guarantees no breaking changes and prevents unwanted streak modifications on app start or close. I\'m focusing on the initial hydration process to ensure a smooth transition from existing data points, specifically from daily and profile data, to ensure a solid and reliable foundation.\n\n\n**Defining Streak Calculation**\n\nI\'ve refined the streak increment logic. Completion on a single date, like November 23rd, 2026, counts only once, deduplicated by the local date key in the YYYY-MM-DD format. I\'m handling missed days: if the user last completed on November 21st and completes on November 23rd, the streak dynamically starts at 0, while the best streak persists. I\'m also ensuring a new personal record is detected when current streak surpasses the previous best streak, even on the first-ever streak.\n\n\n**Refining Animation Trigger**\n\nI\'ve decided to trigger the celebration animation when a new personal record is achieved; specifically, when `currentStreak > prevBest`. Even for a brand new player, this provides immediate gratification on Day 1 (if the previous best is 0) or Day 2 (if they beat a 1-day streak). To prevent re-firing, I\'m storing `lastRecordDate` and `lastRecordStreak`. I\'m also planning the logic to build a 30-day activity calendar.\n\n\n\n**Visualizing Upcoming Calendar**\n\nI\'m now determining how to display a 30-day activity calendar. Should I show the current local calendar month or a rolling 30-day window? I\'m leaning toward the latter for its clarity: it always presents \"Completed,\" \"Missed,\" and \"Upcoming\" states, no matter the date. For example, the 30-day rolling activity window would show past days as either \"Completed\" or \"Missed,\" today as \"Active\" with its status, and future days as \"Upcoming.\" Month and year markers will be used when appropriate.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Milestones**\n\nI\'m now integrating milestone indicators into the daily calendar, specifically for days 3, 7, 14, and 30 of a streak. These will be visually distinct markers on the calendar. I\'m also planning the visualization for the daily entries. \"Completed\" gets a glowing active ring with a checkmark. \"Pending\" has a pulsing cyan outline. Future days are marked as \"Upcoming\" with a soft indigo outline, which also shows milestone markers as appropriate. Additionally, I plan to display month and year indicators for clarity.\n\n**Designing Milestone Display**\n\nI\'m now detailing the visual representation of streak milestones (3, 7, 14, and 30 days). Each will clearly show its state: \"Reached,\" \"In-Progress,\" or \"Locked,\" using icons and text, not just color, with a progress bar. The \"bestStreak\" badge is also being incorporated. I\'m also conceptualizing a neon flame animation that scales with the `currentStreak` intensity, utilizing custom SVG and CSS, and scaling the glow. It includes animated visual indicators that change based on the user\'s progress.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Sound & Animations**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new sound system, upgrading the audio engine to a shared `sfxGain` node. Every sound effect will connect to this node, for volume control. I\'m also planning the new streak record celebration: a neon modal/banner animation, and an inline banner in the Streaks tab.\n\n\n**Refining Audio Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new audio system. I\'m focusing on smooth volume transitions by using Web Audio\'s `setTargetAtTime` function to prevent pops. I\'m also ensuring the default volume is 70% with a range of 0-100%, and storing settings using existing local persistence, including handling for corruption. The new setup guarantees separate control from background music.\n\n\n**Finalizing Audio Integration**\n\nI\'ve just added versioned audio persistence (`neon_block_audio_v1`) to handle volume and mute states, with migration logic from older settings. There\'s also robust validation to handle corrupted data. I\'ve also implemented a live sound preview using a pleasant chime, triggered by the slider or preview button, with throttling to prevent spam. I\'m exploring mute logic during sound preview.\n\n\n**Designing Audio Interactions**\n\nI\'m now detailing audio interactions, focusing on mute states. I\'m prioritizing user experience: dragging the volume slider above 0% should automatically unmute, while the explicit mute toggle functions independently. I\'m also planning a new Audio Settings panel in both the title menu and the pause menu, and the sidebar, for constant volume adjustability.\n\n\n**Adding Dashboard Streak Tab**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"Streaks\" tab to the dashboard, ensuring a clear navigation pathway. Now, I\'m integrating a 7-day streak mini-chart with a direct link to the full streaks view, aligning with the overview, milestones, combos, and achievements. My focus is on providing concise, accessible information at a glance.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new \"Streaks\" tab into the dashboard, ensuring consistent navigation alongside existing features. This includes adding \"STREAKS\" to `DashboardTab`, and `AudioSettingsState` to `src/game/types.ts`. I\'m also preparing to create or modify `/src/ui/components/` files to support the new features, including the neon flame animation. I\'m focusing on preserving functionality and data integrity.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now defining the data structures for managing streaks and audio. This involves implementing types like `StreakSource`, `StreakSaveState`, and `StreakCalendarDay` for the streak engine, and handling the audio engine with `NeonAudioEngine`. I\'m also ensuring the correct versioning for streak and audio data in local storage. My focus is on robust data management and preservation.\n\n\n\n**Adding Visual Flair**\n\nI\'m now adding visual enhancements. Specifically, I\'m integrating the neon flame animations and custom CSS for the slider, including `prefers-reduced-motion` support. I\'m building a multi-layered, animated SVG neon flame indicator that scales based on streak tier. I\'m also creating the Audio Settings UI, including slider, D-pad control, and preview.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "bx4Ea661CZ29sOIP1cuwmAk"
    tool_calls {
