    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport fs from \'fs\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [\n      react(),\n      tailwindcss(),\n      // Copies src/assets into dist/ so root-relative URLs like\n      // \"/src/assets/images/...\" (e.g. generate_image output) still resolve\n      // in production builds. Do not remove.\n      {\n        name: \'copy-unbundled-src-assets\',\n        apply: \'build\',\n        closeBundle(error?: Error): void {\n          if (error) {\n            return;\n          }\n          const distDir = path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\');\n          const srcAssets = path.resolve(__dirname, \'src/assets\');\n          const distAssets = path.resolve(distDir, \'src/assets\');\n          if (fs.existsSync(distDir) && fs.existsSync(srcAssets)) {\n            fs.cpSync(srcAssets, distAssets, {recursive: true, force: true});\n          }\n        },\n      },\n    ],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Create a complete, polished HTML5 Canvas puzzle game called **NEON BLOCK**.\n\nThe game should be an original combination of a tile-merging puzzle and a block-placement puzzle.\n\n**Core requirements:**\n- Single-player offline gameplay.\n- Responsive landscape-first design for Android tablets.\n- Dark background with premium neon graphics.\n- Smooth animations and satisfying visual effects.\n- Touchscreen support.\n- Keyboard arrow keys, Enter and Space support.\n- Prepare controls for future Amazon Fire TV D-pad compatibility.\n- Score, best score and game-over screen.\n- Save high scores locally.\n- Pause, restart and sound toggle.\n- Generate sound effects using Web Audio API.\n- No external APIs, external CDNs, login or online dependencies.\n- No Google Play Services.\n\n**Design:**\nCreate a premium arcade interface with glowing blue, purple and cyan tiles, clean typography, subtle gradients and polished transitions.\n\n**Technical requirements:**\n- Use HTML5 Canvas and JavaScript.\n- Keep the game self-contained.\n- Do not use copyrighted game assets.\n- Handle different screen sizes without clipping.\n- Include clear instructions for players.\n- Make all buttons functional.\n- Avoid placeholder functionality.\n\nBuild the complete playable game, not just a prototype or visual mockup.\n\nBefore finishing, test the game logic, tile movement, scoring, collision detection, game-over conditions and restart functionality."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Upgrade the existing NEON BLOCK game. Do not rebuild or remove existing gameplay functionality.\n\nAdd the following features:\n\n1. DAILY CHALLENGE SYSTEM\n- Generate a new challenge based on the local calendar date.\n- Include daily objectives, difficulty levels and rewards.\n- Add a daily streak counter.\n- Save challenge completion and progress locally.\n- Prevent accidental duplicate rewards.\n- Provide a dedicated Daily Challenge screen.\n\n2. ADVANCED PARTICLE VISUAL EFFECTS\n- Neon particle bursts when tiles merge.\n- Colorful particle explosions for combos.\n- Glowing shockwaves when clearing lines.\n- Floating particles in the background.\n- High-score celebration with fireworks.\n- Smooth fade-out and particle animations.\n- Optimize particle counts for mobile performance.\n\n3. POLISH\n- Add smooth screen transitions.\n- Add subtle screen shake for major combos.\n- Include particle intensity settings.\n- Add sound effects synchronized with visual effects.\n- Respect reduced-motion preferences.\n\nMaintain offline functionality. Do not introduce external APIs, online dependencies or third-party asset requirements.\n\nKeep all existing scoring, controls, saved records and gameplay logic working. Test all new features before completion."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Upgrade the existing NEON BLOCK game into a premium arcade puzzle experience.\n\nIMPORTANT: Preserve all existing gameplay mechanics, scoring, controls, animations, particle effects, Daily Challenge and saved data. Do not rebuild the game from scratch.\n\nAdd the following systems:\n\n1. DAILY REWARD MILESTONES\n- Create a 30-day daily reward progression.\n- Add rewards at days 1, 3, 5, 7, 14 and 30.\n- Include bonus points, cosmetic themes and particle effects.\n- Add a reward claim animation.\n- Add a streak indicator and milestone progress bar.\n- Save claimed rewards locally.\n- Prevent duplicate reward claims.\n- Handle date changes and streak resets correctly.\n\n2. COMBO HISTORY\n- Record every significant combo event.\n- Track highest combo multiplier.\n- Track total combos.\n- Track highest single-combo score.\n- Display the latest 20 combo events.\n- Include combo statistics and personal records.\n- Add a clear history option with confirmation.\n\n3. PLAYER PROGRESSION\n- Add XP and player levels.\n- Award XP for completed games, combos and challenges.\n- Add achievement badges.\n- Add unlockable visual themes.\n- Save all progression locally.\n\n4. DASHBOARD\nCreate a polished statistics dashboard with:\n- Current player level.\n- XP progress bar.\n- Daily streak.\n- Reward milestones.\n- Best combo.\n- Total combos.\n- Achievement collection.\n- Recently unlocked rewards.\n\n5. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS\n- Fully offline.\n- Use localStorage with versioned data and safe migration.\n- Validate saved data.\n- Handle missing or corrupted storage gracefully.\n- Use the device\'s local date consistently.\n- Prevent reward duplication.\n- Avoid excessive animations and memory usage.\n- Keep the interface responsive on Android tablets.\n\nDo not use external APIs, accounts, cloud databases or external dependencies.\n\nTest all features and ensure existing gameplay continues working without regressions."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Add a dedicated \'How to Play\' help menu modal overlay trigger for the \'H\' key and make the \'Escape\' key return the user to the previous menu state across all views."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Update the DashboardScreen to include a visual sparkline or mini-bar chart that displays the player\'s 7-day streak history, showing which days they completed the challenge to visualize their consistency."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Upgrade the existing NEON BLOCK game by adding two features: ADVANCED STREAK VISUALIZATION and SOUND EFFECT VOLUME CONTROL.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not rebuild the game.\nDo not remove or modify existing gameplay mechanics, scoring, daily challenges, daily rewards, combo history, achievements, XP, particle effects or saved progress.\n\nFEATURE 1: STREAK VISUALIZATION\n\nCreate a premium streak dashboard.\n\nInclude:\n- Current daily streak.\n- Best-ever streak.\n- Animated neon flame indicator.\n- Seven-day activity visualization.\n- Thirty-day activity calendar.\n- Completed-day, missed-day and upcoming-day states.\n- Milestone indicators for 3, 7, 14 and 30 consecutive days.\n- Celebration animation when a new personal streak record is reached.\n\nSTREAK LOGIC:\n- Use the device\'s local calendar date.\n- Count a streak only when the player completes the existing daily challenge or qualifies through the existing daily reward system.\n- Never increment a streak multiple times on the same calendar day.\n- Preserve the best-ever streak when the current streak resets.\n- Handle month changes, year changes and app restarts correctly.\n- Do not reset streaks merely because the app is opened or closed.\n- Avoid conflicting with existing daily challenge and reward logic.\n\nFEATURE 2: SOUND EFFECT VOLUME CONTROL\n\nAdd an audio settings panel.\n\nInclude:\n- Sound effects volume slider from 0 to 100%.\n- Mute and unmute toggle.\n- Live sound preview.\n- Default volume of 70%.\n- Persist the selected volume locally.\n- Restore the selected volume after restarting the application.\n- Smooth volume transitions without sudden audio pops.\n- Ensure every game sound effect respects the selected volume.\n- If the game uses Web Audio API, route sound effects through a shared GainNode.\n\nIf background music already exists, preserve its existing functionality and avoid unintentionally changing it when the user adjusts sound effect volume.\n\nDESIGN:\n- Match the existing NEON BLOCK dark neon visual identity.\n- Use cyan, purple and blue highlights.\n- Add smooth transitions and subtle animations.\n- Ensure large, accessible touch controls.\n- Maintain landscape tablet compatibility.\n- Prepare navigation controls for Fire TV remote compatibility.\n\nTECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n- Fully offline.\n- Use existing local persistence architecture.\n- Avoid external APIs and dependencies.\n- Handle missing or corrupted saved settings gracefully.\n- Preserve all existing stored player data.\n\nFINAL REGRESSION TEST:\nTest streak calculations, duplicate daily claims, month changes, year changes, reward synchronization, volume adjustment, mute/unmute, sound playback after restarting, and all existing gameplay features.\n\nDo not leave placeholder buttons or incomplete functionality.\n\nReturn the complete updated project and report the tests performed."
    }
  }
}
