    thinking: "**Analyzing User Request Details**\n\nI\'m meticulously dissecting User Request #7, focusing intently on Feature 1, the streak visualization within the premium dashboard. I\'m cross-referencing this against the dashboard screen\'s design to pinpoint potential integration issues. Every edge case and nuance is under review, focusing on the `STREAKS` tab.\n\n\n**Expanding Streak Implementation Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the scope to integrate the streak data across the `Overview`, `Sidebar`, `Title Menu`, and `DailyChallengeScreen`, not just the premium dashboard. I\'ve broken down the data points: the current daily streak (`unifiedCurrentStreak`), the best-ever streak (`unifiedBestStreak`), the animated neon flame indicator (`NeonFlame`), and seven-day activity visualisations with sparklines and bar charts, as well as the thirty-day calendar. I\'m focusing on those month and year boundaries in the calendar now!\n\n\n**Implementing Streak Record Animation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the celebratory animation. Upon a new personal streak record, I plan to trigger `neonAudio.playStreakRecord()`, `canvasHandleRef.current?.triggerFireworks(7)` (respecting `reducedMotion`), and a new \"Streak Record Celebration Modal\" within `App.tsx`. I need to ensure this modal includes `<NeonFlame size=\"lg\" />`, animated neon elements, and clear display of streak details. I\'m also going back to validate an edge case in `streaks.ts`.\n\n\n**Tracing Streak Logic Flow**\n\nI\'m now tracing the logic for calculating and updating streak records. I\'ve walked through the scenarios for a new player. On day one, the initial record calculation triggers a new record, which then properly handles the daily bonus. Subsequent days maintain and update streak data. I\'ve verified that the math for a brand new player functions as intended with those two edge cases.\n\n\n**Validating Streak Break Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now deeply focused on edge cases where streaks are broken and need to ensure the system handles them gracefully. I am simulating a user journey, with the app closed, reopened, and days missed. It\'s imperative that the daily streak resets properly upon a missed day, while retaining the best streak achieved. I am confident that the current logic correctly determines a new record only when a new best streak is calculated, and correctly triggers celebrations! I\'m now testing clock rollback scenarios.\n\n\n**Verifying Data Integrity**\n\nI\'m now back-checking `validateAndHydrateStreakState` in `streaks.ts`, specifically lines 204-214, after considering a potential date discrepancy in the logic. I am particularly concerned with migrating pre-existing saved progress. I\'m focusing on the backfilling logic for reward streak dates and how it merges with any existing sources. I\'m satisfied that edge cases with earlier dates have been validated. Now, I am exploring migration paths from previous game builds.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Z-Index Priorities**\n\nI\'m now refining the modal z-index priorities to ensure a smooth user experience. My focus is on the potential simultaneous display of `claimCelebration` from `DashboardScreen.tsx` and `streakRecordCelebration` from `App.tsx` when a daily reward triggers a new streak record. I\'m exploring modal layering so that `streakRecordCelebration` is always on top. I also plan to make sure Escape key behavior dismisses modals in the correct order.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Modal Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the deterministic modal layering and escape key behavior. `streakRecordCelebration` (z-50) will sit above `showAudioSettings` (z-45), `showHelp` (z-40), and then the internal `claimCelebration` from the `DashboardScreen` (z-30). View navigation remains the lowest priority. The Escape key now correctly dismisses the modals in the defined, precise order.\n\n\n**Optimizing TV D-pad Control**\n\nI\'ve been refining sound setting interaction on Fire TV. I\'m leaning toward a `step={1}` range input with `onKeyDown` listeners to accelerate arrow key navigation to +/-5%. This offers both granular touch control and ergonomic D-pad adjustments, optimizing for Fire TV use. I\'m also planning a mute/unmute toggle, which I will add to the settings panel.\n\n\n**Implementing Volume Mute Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the mute logic for the audio settings panel across multiple UI components. I\'ve considered that if a muted user adjusts volume, the system should automatically unmute, providing immediate sound feedback. The mute setting now cleanly preserves saved volume levels, allowing for accurate restoration. I\'m also implementing live sound previews triggered by volume changes.\n\n\n**Refining Volume Persistence Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the audio persistence logic to ensure smooth volume transitions. I\'ve focused on `audio.ts`, particularly lines 95-112, to anchor `param.value` before calling `setTargetAtTime`. I\'ve added a fallback to `setValueAtTime(param.value, now)` for compatibility. I\'m also addressing the migration to the new `neon_block_audio_v1` format to ensure backwards compatibility with older save data. I\'m verifying local storage access.\n\n\n"
