  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing App Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the changes into `src/App.tsx` using `multi_replace_file_content`. I\'m meticulously double-checking line numbers and exact content targets within the file (lines 1-1564), and I\'m reviewing every piece I\'m about to update to ensure accuracy.\n\n\n**Adding New Imports**\n\nI\'ve just added several new imports to `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve added `SlidersHorizontal`, `Trophy` (and potentially `Volume1`) from `lucide-react`, and `AudioSettingsPanel`, `NeonFlame`, and `getFlameTierLabel` from local components. I\'ve also integrated audio functions and streak-related state management, while eliminating some unused imports. The focus is on streamlining the core application logic.\n\n\n**Integrating Audio & Streak**\n\nI\'m now integrating audio settings and streak state management. I\'ve initialized `dailyState`, `profile`, and `streakState`, ensuring `streakState` loads existing data without resetting streaks. I\'m also adding `streakStateRef`. I\'m focusing on callbacks for streak qualification, and I\'m adding `commitStreakState` and `recordStreakQualification`. This includes recording qualifying days and persisting the state. If it\'s a new record, the code now triggers fireworks and plays a celebratory audio cue, via `neonAudio.playStreakRecord`. The `handleStatsChange` now calls `recordStreakQualification` too.\n\n\n**Refining Streak Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the streak logic further. Before `recordDailyChallengeVictoryProgression`, I\'m passing the best streak. I\'m also ensuring the best streak is checked in several functions, including `handleTurnResolved`, `handleClaimDailyMilestone`, and `handleGameOver`. When `res.claimed` in `handleClaimDailyMilestone`, I\'m calling `recordStreakQualification`. I\'ve added `handleSfxVolumeChange` to manage audio volume, including clamping, auto-unmuting on drag, sound preview, and configuration updates, while updating `toggleMute` as well.\n\n\n**Enhancing Audio and Controls**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `handlePreviewSound`, and ensuring `neonAudio.unlock()` gets called. I\'ve integrated functions to manage various UI states, including `openAudioSettings`, `closeAudioSettings`, and `closeStreakCelebration`. The auto-focus effect is updated, now focusing the close button correctly in different panels.\n\n**Introducing a Global Keyboard Handler**\n\nI\'m adding a global keyboard handler. The Escape key now works correctly to dismiss menus, even when focusing `<input type=\"range\">`. I\'ve added a layer of Escape priority. The Enter/Space keys dismiss the `streakCelebration` panel unless a button is selected. Finally, I\'ve updated the guard to allow opening audio and streaks through the keyboard.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the changes into various UI elements. I\'m focusing on the Title Menu, Dashboard, Pause Modal, Audio Settings Modal, and Streak Record Celebration Modal. I\'m making the streak readout clickable in the Title Menu to open the Dashboard. I\'m unifying the best streak calculation, using `unifiedCurrentStreak` as `displayStreak` across HUD, Title Menu, and Game Over. In the Portrait/Mobile Header, the speaker button now opens Audio Settings, and I\'m adding clickable functionality to open the Audio Settings from the Landscape Sidebar. I\'m also ensuring the `<NeonCanvas />` status correctly reflects the paused state when various panels are open.\n\n\n**Adding Title Menu Audio & Streak**\n\nI\'m working on integrating a concise audio settings control directly into the Title Menu\'s metadata area. I\'m adding display of the best streak to the menu as well. I\'m passing `streakState`, `sfxVolume`, `muted`, and other related props to the `DashboardScreen`, and I\'m updating the Pause Modal to embed a compact `AudioSettingsPanel`. Also, I\'m adding an Audio Settings Modal and a Streak Record Celebration Modal.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "tyMEa6H5B5XG-8YPipXlWQ"
    tool_calls {
